---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Styleguide
description: Reference for the HRJ site design system — tokens, type, layout primitives and every component, with copyable markup.
pageCss: styleguide
noindex: true
sitemap: false
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#-
  KITCHEN SINK. Page builders: copy markup from here. Each pattern below is the
  canonical version; the grey "source" blocks show the exact HTML.
-#}
{%- macro source(markup) -%}
<pre class="sg-code"><code>{{ markup | trim | forceescape }}</code></pre>
{%- endmacro -%}

<header class="page-hero">
  <div class="container page-hero__inner">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li><span aria-current="page">Styleguide</span></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    <p class="eyebrow">Design system · v2</p>
    <h1 class="page-hero__title">Field notebook <em>styleguide</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">Every token and component in <code>main.css</code>, rendered with real markup. Copy patterns from here; don’t re-implement buttons, cards or labels in page CSS.</p>
    <dl class="ledger page-hero__meta">
      <div><dt>Stylesheet</dt><dd>/assets/css/main.css — layers: reset, tokens, base, layout, components, page, utilities</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Docs</dt><dd>docs/DESIGN.md §4–6 and §10</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>Not indexed (noindex), not in the sitemap</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</header>

<nav class="sg-nav" aria-label="Styleguide sections">
  <div class="container">
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#colour">Colour</a></li>
      <li><a href="#type">Type</a></li>
      <li><a href="#space">Space</a></li>
      <li><a href="#layout">Layout</a></li>
      <li><a href="#actions">Actions</a></li>
      <li><a href="#icons">Icons</a></li>
      <li><a href="#cards">Cards</a></li>
      <li><a href="#tags">Tags</a></li>
      <li><a href="#data">Ledger · stats</a></li>
      <li><a href="#timeline">Timeline</a></li>
      <li><a href="#logos">Logo row</a></li>
      <li><a href="#patterns">Shared patterns</a></li>
      <li><a href="#quote">Quote</a></li>
      <li><a href="#notices">Notices</a></li>
      <li><a href="#media">Media</a></li>
      <li><a href="#forms">Forms</a></li>
      <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
      <li><a href="#heroes">Page hero</a></li>
      <li><a href="#gallery">Gallery</a></li>
      <li><a href="#bands">Dark bands</a></li>
      <li><a href="#hiti">Hiti diagram</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</nav>

{# ======================================================================= #}
<section class="sg-section" id="colour">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Colour</h2>
    <p class="sg-intro">Brick is for primary actions and heritage emphasis (one primary button per view). Copper is for links, water and focus. Gilt is decorative only on light surfaces — use <code>--gilt-text</code> for gold-toned text. <code>--ink-3</code> is the minimum for any text on light. Ratios are WCAG 2.2 contrast against <code>--paper</code> (light) or <code>--soot</code> (dark).</p>
    {%- set swatches = [
      ["paper", "#f3ede1", "Page background."],
      ["paper-2", "#ebe3d3", "Alternate band (.section--alt)."],
      ["card", "#fbf8f2", "Raised surfaces, inputs. Ink on card 16.2:1."],
      ["rule", "#cfc4ae", "Decorative hairlines only — 1.5:1."],
      ["field-border", "#8f8270", "Input and chip borders — 3.2:1 (non-text)."],
      ["ink", "#1f1b16", "Body and headings — 14.7:1."],
      ["ink-2", "#4a4237", "Secondary text — 8.5:1."],
      ["ink-3", "#675c4b", "Captions, labels — 5.6:1 (5.1 on paper-2). Minimum for text."],
      ["brick", "#9c3f26", "Primary button bg, heritage accent text — 5.7:1. Card text on brick 6.3:1."],
      ["brick-hover", "#84341f", "Primary hover — 7.2:1."],
      ["copper", "#33604f", "Links, water accent, focus ring — 6.2:1."],
      ["gilt-text", "#7d5f17", "Gold-toned text on light — 5.1:1 (4.7 on paper-2: large text only there)."],
      ["gilt", "#b08a2e", "Decorative only on light — 2.8:1, never text."],
      ["brick-tint", "#f2e2d9", "Heritage tag bg. Brick on it 5.3:1."],
      ["copper-tint", "#dfe9e3", "Water tag / success bg. Copper on it 5.8:1."],
      ["gilt-tint", "#f1e6c8", "Education tag / info bg. Gilt-text on it 4.8:1."],
      ["soot", "#1c1915", "Dark band background."],
      ["soot-2", "#26221c", "Raised surface on dark."],
      ["lime", "#efe8d8", "Text on dark — 14.4:1."],
      ["lime-2", "#c4b89e", "Secondary on dark — 8.9:1."],
      ["lime-3", "#a39579", "Captions on dark — 6.0:1."],
      ["gilt-on-dark", "#d4b25a", "Links, accents, focus on dark — 8.6:1."],
      ["terra-on-dark", "#e08a68", "Heritage accent on dark — 6.7:1."],
      ["patina-on-dark", "#8cc0a6", "Water accent on dark — 8.5:1."]
    ] -%}
    <ul class="sg-swatches">
      {%- for s in swatches %}
      <li class="sg-swatch" data-token="{{ s[0] }}">
        <div class="sg-swatch__chip"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch__body">
          <span class="sg-swatch__name">--{{ s[0] }}</span>
          <span class="sg-swatch__value">{{ s[1] }}</span>
          <span class="sg-swatch__note">{{ s[2] }}</span>
        </div>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="sg-note mt-m">Components use semantic aliases (--surface, --text, --text-2, --text-3, --line, --line-strong, --link, --focus, --accent, --accent-water, --accent-gold, --decor). Dark bands remap only these.</p>
  </div>
</section>

{# ======================================================================= #}
<section class="sg-section" id="type">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Type</h2>
    <p class="sg-intro">Fraunces for headings and the wordmark, Public Sans for body and UI, JetBrains Mono for field-note labels, Tiro Devanagari Hindi for Newar and Nepali terms. Use only the scale steps below (utility classes <code>.fs--1</code> … <code>.fs-5</code>).</p>

    <div class="sg-scale">
      <div class="sg-scale__row"><span class="sg-note">--step-5 · home hero</span><span class="sg-scale__sample fs-5">Engineering the ancient</span></div>
      <div class="sg-scale__row"><span class="sg-note">--step-4 · page h1</span><span class="sg-scale__sample fs-4">Water that still flows</span></div>
      <div class="sg-scale__row"><span class="sg-note">--step-3 · h2</span><span class="sg-scale__sample fs-3">Selected work</span></div>
      <div class="sg-scale__row"><span class="sg-note">--step-2 · h3</span><span class="sg-scale__sample fs-2">Alko Hiti reconstruction</span></div>
      <div class="sg-scale__row"><span class="sg-note">--step-1 · lead / h4</span><span class="fs-1">A lede paragraph sits at step 1 in ink-2.</span></div>
      <div class="sg-scale__row"><span class="sg-note">--step-0 · body</span><span class="fs-0">Body copy, 1.65 line-height, measure ≤ 68ch.</span></div>
      <div class="sg-scale__row"><span class="sg-note">--step--1 · small</span><span class="fs--1">Captions, card text, form hints.</span></div>
      <div class="sg-scale__row"><span class="sg-note">--label · mono</span><span class="label">Mono label · 0.78rem · uppercase</span></div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="sg-h3">Headings, eyebrow, lede, Devanagari</h3>
    {% set typeDemo %}
<div class="stack stack--s">
  <p class="eyebrow">Heritage engineering</p>
  <h2>Hiti stone-spout systems</h2>
  <p class="lede">Living hydraulic infrastructure, still carrying water after 1,500 years.</p>
  <p>The <span class="deva" lang="new">नाभिमण्डल</span> (nabhi mandal) calms the spring’s pressure before water reaches the spout.</p>
</div>
    {% endset %}
    <div class="sg-frame">{{ typeDemo | safe }}</div>
    {{ source(typeDemo) }}
    <p class="sg-note mt-s">Eyebrow variants: <code>.eyebrow--plain</code> (no rule), <code>.eyebrow--water</code>, <code>.eyebrow--heritage</code>. Generic mono label: <code>.label</code>.</p>

    <h3 class="sg-h3">Prose (Markdown body)</h3>
    <div class="sg-frame">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>How a hiti works</h2>
        <p>Water from an aquifer travels through <a href="#type">underground channels</a> into a stepped, sunken courtyard. The spout itself — the <em>ga hiti</em> — is often carved as a <strong>makara</strong>, a mythical water creature.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Source: spring or pond recharge</li>
          <li>Conveyance: <code>hiti duun</code> conduit</li>
          <li>Outlet: stone spout</li>
        </ul>
        <blockquote><p>The hiti is not a relic. It is a functioning technology.</p></blockquote>
        <h3>Measured data</h3>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Spout</th><th>Discharge</th><th>Season</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody><tr><td>Example A</td><td>0.4 L/s</td><td>Dry</td></tr><tr><td>Example B</td><td>1.1 L/s</td><td>Monsoon</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
        <hr>
        <ol><li>Survey</li><li>Calculate</li><li>Draw</li></ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ======================================================================= #}
<section class="sg-section" id="space">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Space, shape, motion</h2>
    <p class="sg-intro">Spacing tokens, radii (<code>--radius-s 4px</code>, <code>--radius 8px</code>, <code>--radius-l 14px</code>), one paper shadow (<code>--shadow</code>), <code>--ease</code> with 150/250/400ms. Section padding is <code>--section-pad</code>. All motion is disabled under reduced motion.</p>
    <div class="sg-space">
      {%- for s in ["3xs", "2xs", "xs", "s", "m", "l", "xl", "2xl", "3xl"] %}
      <div class="sg-space__row"><span class="sg-note">--space-{{ s }}</span><span class="sg-space__bar" data-space="{{ s }}"></span></div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ======================================================================= #}
<section class="sg-section" id="layout">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Layout primitives</h2>
    <p class="sg-intro"><code>.container</code> (72rem) / <code>--narrow</code> (46rem) / <code>--wide</code> (86rem). <code>.section</code>, <code>.section--alt</code>, <code>.section--tight</code>. Base margins are zero — use <code>.stack</code> (with <code>--2xs … --2xl</code>) or <code>.prose</code> for vertical rhythm.</p>

    <h3 class="sg-h3">.stack · .cluster</h3>
    {% set stackDemo %}
<div class="stack stack--xs">
  <div class="sg-box">.stack child</div>
  <div class="sg-box">.stack child</div>
</div>
<div class="cluster mt-m">
  <span class="sg-box">.cluster</span><span class="sg-box">wraps</span><span class="sg-box">with gap</span>
</div>
    {% endset %}
    <div class="sg-frame">{{ stackDemo | safe }}</div>
    {{ source(stackDemo) }}
    <p class="sg-note mt-s">.cluster modifiers: --tight, --loose, --between, --baseline.</p>

    <h3 class="sg-h3">.grid--2 / --3 / --4</h3>
    <div class="sg-frame stack stack--m">
      <div class="grid grid--2"><div class="sg-box">grid--2</div><div class="sg-box">grid--2</div></div>
      <div class="grid grid--3"><div class="sg-box">grid--3</div><div class="sg-box">grid--3</div><div class="sg-box">grid--3</div></div>
      <div class="grid grid--4"><div class="sg-box">grid--4</div><div class="sg-box">grid--4</div><div class="sg-box">grid--4</div><div class="sg-box">grid--4</div></div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="sg-h3">.split (text + media, stacks below 52rem)</h3>
    {% set splitDemo %}
<div class="split">
  <div class="stack stack--s">
    <p class="eyebrow">Split</p>
    <h3>Text column</h3>
    <p>Modifiers: <code>.split--reverse</code>, <code>.split--media-wide</code>, <code>.split--text-wide</code>, <code>.split--top</code>.</p>
  </div>
  {% media "", "", { kind: "heritage", ratio: "4/3" } %}
</div>
    {% endset %}
    <div class="sg-frame">{{ splitDemo | safe }}</div>

    <h3 class="sg-h3">.with-aside (detail pages)</h3>
    <div class="sg-frame">
      <div class="with-aside">
        <div class="with-aside__main sg-box">.with-aside__main — prose, gallery…</div>
        <aside class="with-aside__aside sg-box">.with-aside__aside — sticky ledger (≥ 60rem)</aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ======================================================================= #}
<section class="sg-section" id="actions">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Buttons and links</h2>
    <p class="sg-intro">Min target 44px. One <code>.btn--primary</code> per view. Focus is a 2px copper outline (gilt on dark).</p>
    {% set btnDemo %}
<div class="cluster">
  <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#actions">Work with me{% icon "arrow-right" %}</a>
  <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="#actions">View the work</a>
  <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="#actions" download>{% icon "download" %}Download CV</a>
  <button class="btn btn--primary btn--small" type="button">Small</button>
  <button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" disabled>Disabled</button>
  <button class="btn btn--secondary" type="button" disabled>Disabled</button>
  <a class="link-arrow" href="#actions">All projects{% icon "arrow-right" %}</a>
  <a class="link-arrow" href="#actions">{% icon "arrow-left" %}Back to work</a>
</div>
    {% endset %}
    <div class="sg-frame">{{ btnDemo | safe }}</div>
    {{ source('<a class="btn btn--primary" href="/work-with-me/">Work with me{% icon "arrow-right" %}</a>\n<a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/work/">View the work</a>\n<a class="link-arrow" href="/work/">All projects{% icon "arrow-right" %}</a>') }}
    <div class="band--dark sg-frame mt-m">
      <div class="cluster">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#actions">Primary on dark</a>
        <a class="btn btn--on-dark" href="#actions">.btn--on-dark</a>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="#actions">Link on dark{% icon "arrow-right" %}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ======================================================================= #}
<section class="sg-section" id="icons">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Icons</h2>
    <p class="sg-intro"><code>{{ '{% icon "name" %}' }}</code> or <code>{{ '{% icon "name", "icon--l" %}' }}</code> → inline SVG, <code>aria-hidden</code>, <code>currentColor</code>, 1.5 stroke. Size follows the font (1.15em); <code>.icon--s</code>, <code>.icon--l</code>.</p>
    <ul class="sg-icons">
      {%- for name in ["arrow-right", "arrow-left", "arrow-up-right", "chevron-down", "chevron-left", "chevron-right", "download", "mail", "whatsapp", "phone", "map-pin", "linkedin", "medium", "menu", "close", "water", "heritage", "robot", "walk", "pen", "calendar", "users", "clock", "globe", "check", "plus", "minus"] %}
      <li>{% icon name %}{{ name }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

{# ======================================================================= #}
<section class="sg-section section--alt" id="cards">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Cards</h2>
    <p class="sg-intro"><code>.card--link</code>: the whole card is clickable through the <strong>title link’s ::after overlay</strong>. Never wrap a card in <code>&lt;a&gt;</code>. Thumbnails in link cards use <code>alt=""</code> (the title names the card). Optional <code>data-domain="water|heritage|education"</code> adds a coloured top rule. Placeholders shown for every media <code>kind</code>.</p>

    {% set cardDemo %}
<article class="card card--link" data-domain="heritage">
  <div class="card__media">
    {% media "/assets/images/work/example/cover.jpg", "", { ratio: "3/2", kind: "heritage" } %}
  </div>
  <div class="card__body">
    <p class="card__meta"><span>Heritage</span><span>2022–present</span></p>
    <h3 class="card__title"><a href="#cards">Hiti stone-spout systems</a></h3>
    <p class="card__text">Measured cross-sections of the Valley’s living water spouts.</p>
    <div class="card__footer">
      <span class="card__cue" aria-hidden="true">Read the case study{% icon "arrow-right" %}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
    {% endset %}

    <div class="grid grid--3">
      {{ cardDemo | safe }}
      {%- set kinds = [["photo", "Photo", "water", "Groundwater recharge, Balaju"], ["drawing", "Drawing", "heritage", "Measured hiti section"], ["water", "Water", "water", "Rajkulo canal survey"], ["walk", "Walk", "heritage", "Patan water walk"], ["robotics", "Robotics", "education", "Yala Mayor’s Cup"], ["map", "Map", "water", "Canal route map"], ["portrait", "Portrait", "", "Portrait placeholder"]] %}
      {%- for k in kinds %}
      <article class="card card--link"{% if k[2] %} data-domain="{{ k[2] }}"{% endif %}>
        <div class="card__media">{% media "", "", { ratio: "3/2", kind: k[0] } %}</div>
        <div class="card__body">
          <p class="card__meta"><span>kind: {{ k[0] }}</span>{% if k[2] %}<span>{{ k[2] }}</span>{% endif %}</p>
          <h3 class="card__title"><a href="#cards">{{ k[3] }}</a></h3>
          <p class="card__text">Placeholder line-art for <code>kind: "{{ k[0] }}"</code>.</p>
          <div class="card__footer"><ul class="tags" role="list"><li class="tag tag--{{ 'education' if k[2] == 'education' else ('heritage' if k[2] == 'heritage' else 'water') }}">{{ k[1] }}</li></ul></div>
        </div>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    {{ source(cardDemo) }}

    <h3 class="sg-h3">Static card and .card--plain</h3>
    <div class="grid grid--3">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card__body">
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--water">Service</p>
          <h3 class="card__title">Groundwater recharge studies</h3>
          <p class="card__text">A static card (no link) — services, notes, contact blocks.</p>
          <div class="card__footer"><a class="link-arrow" href="#cards">Ask about this{% icon "arrow-right" %}</a></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card card--plain">
        <div class="card__body">
          <p class="card__meta"><span>Setopati English</span><span>Sept 2025</span></p>
          <h3 class="card__title">Flames of September</h3>
          <p class="card__text">.card--plain — top rule only, no surface. Good for lists of writing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card card--plain">
        <div class="card__body">
          <p class="card__meta"><span>Nepali Times</span><span>2022</span></p>
          <h3 class="card__title"><a href="#cards">Kathmandu’s ancient water spouts</a></h3>
          <p class="card__text">Plain card with a normal (non-overlay) title link.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ======================================================================= #}
<section class="sg-section" id="tags">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Tags and chips</h2>
    <p class="sg-intro"><code>.tag</code> is a static label; <code>.chip</code> is a filter toggle button using <code>aria-pressed</code>. Wrap filter UIs in <code>.js-only</code> (they need JS; without it all items show).</p>
    {% set tagDemo %}
<ul class="tags" role="list">
  <li class="tag">Default</li>
  <li class="tag tag--water">Water</li>
  <li class="tag tag--heritage">Heritage</li>
  <li class="tag tag--education">Education</li>
</ul>
<div class="chips js-only mt-m" role="group" aria-label="Filter projects">
  <button class="chip" type="button" aria-pressed="true">All <span class="chip__count">8</span></button>
  <button class="chip" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Water <span class="chip__count">3</span></button>
  <button class="chip" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Heritage <span class="chip__count">4</span></button>
  <button class="chip" type="button" disabled>Archive</button>
</div>
    {% endset %}
    <div class="sg-frame">{{ tagDemo | safe }}</div>
    {{ source(tagDemo) }}
  </div>
</section>

{# ======================================================================= #}
<section class="sg-section" id="data">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Ledger and stats</h2>
    <div class="split split--top">
      <div>
        <h3 class="sg-h3 mt-0">.ledger</h3>
        {% set ledgerDemo %}
<dl class="ledger">
  <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Lead engineer</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Client</dt><dd>Lalitpur Metropolitan City (LMC)</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Location</dt><dd>Mangalbazar, Lalitpur</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Years</dt><dd>2022–present</dd></div>
</dl>
        {% endset %}
        {{ ledgerDemo | safe }}
        {{ source(ledgerDemo) }}
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="sg-h3 mt-0">.stats (from stats.yml)</h3>
        <ul class="stats" role="list">
          {%- for s in stats | limit(4) %}
          <li class="stats__item">
            <span class="stats__value">{{ s.value }}</span>
            <span class="stats__label">{{ s.label }}</span>
            <span class="stats__detail">{{ s.detail }}</span>
          </li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        {{ source('<ul class="stats" role="list">\n  <li class="stats__item">\n    <span class="stats__value">300+</span>\n    <span class="stats__label">students reached</span>\n    <span class="stats__detail">Robotics programme in Lalitpur public schools</span>\n  </li>\n</ul>') }}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ======================================================================= #}
<section class="sg-section section--alt" id="timeline">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>Timeline</h2>
    <p class="sg-intro">A vertical logbook. <code>data-type</code> (engineering | heritage | education | community) colours the dot.</p>
    <ol class="timeline">
      {%- for t in timeline | limit(4) %}
      <li class="timeline__item" data-type="{{ t.type }}">
        <p class="timeline__years">{{ t.years }}</p>
        <h3 class="timeline__role">{{ t.role }}</h3>
        <p class="timeline__org">{{ t.org }}</p>
        <p class="timeline__desc">{{ t.desc }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
    {{ source('<ol class="timeline">\n  <li class="timeline__item" data-type="heritage">\n    <p class="timeline__years">Jun–Dec 2024</p>\n    <h3 class="timeline__role">Technical Advisor, Hiti Reconstruction</h3>\n    <p class="timeline__org">Kathmandu Metropolitan City (KMC)</p>\n    <p class="timeline__desc">…</p>\n  </li>\n</ol>') }}
  </div>
</section>

{# ======================================================================= #}
<section class="sg-section" id="logos">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Logo row and dot list</h2>
    <p class="sg-intro">Institutions as typographic wordmarks, separated by gilt dots; a wrapped line never starts with a dot. For “Worked with and for” always include <code>partials/clients.njk</code> (set <code>clientsLabelledBy</code> to your heading’s id first): it wraps acronyms in <code>&lt;abbr&gt;</code> and adds a visible key. <code>.dot-list</code> is the same separator without the display type. Neither may contain links or buttons.</p>
    <h3 class="label" id="sg-clients-title">Worked with and for</h3>
    {%- set clientsLabelledBy = "sg-clients-title" %}
    {% include "partials/clients.njk" %}
    {{ source('<h2 class="label" id="clients-title">Worked with and for</h2>
{%- set clientsLabelledBy = "clients-title" %}
{% include "partials/clients.njk" %}') }}
    <ul class="dot-list mt-l" role="list"><li>AutoCAD</li><li>Python</li><li>Arduino and mBlock</li><li>Hydraulic discharge calculations</li></ul>
    {{ source('<ul class="dot-list" role="list"><li>AutoCAD</li><li>Python</li></ul>') }}
  </div>
</section>

{# ======================================================================= #}
<section class="sg-section section--alt" id="patterns">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Shared patterns</h2>
    <p class="sg-intro">Small components that pages used to rebuild. <code>data-domain="water|heritage|education"</code> on any element sets <code>--domain</code> (rings, rules) and <code>--domain-text</code> (text, icons) for everything inside it.</p>

    <h3 class="sg-h3">Horizontal and feature cards</h3>
    {% set hCard %}
<article class="card card--link card--horizontal card--feature" data-domain="water">
  <div class="card__media">{% media "", "", { ratio: "3/2", kind: "water" } %}</div>
  <div class="card__body">
    <p class="card__meta"><span>Water engineering</span><span>2022–present</span></p>
    <h3 class="card__title"><a href="#patterns">Media beside the text from 48rem</a></h3>
    <p class="card__text">Add .card--reverse to put the media on the right; set --card-media-min for a taller image.</p>
  </div>
</article>
    {% endset %}
    {{ hCard | safe }}
    {{ source(hCard) }}

    <h3 class="sg-h3">Markers, tick list, label--plain, pointer</h3>
    <div class="grid grid--3">
      <div class="cluster" data-domain="heritage"><span class="marker" aria-hidden="true">01</span><span class="marker marker--icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "check", "icon--l" %}</span></div>
      <ul class="checklist" role="list" data-domain="education"><li>{% icon "check" %}<span>Robotics workshops</span></li><li>{% icon "check" %}<span>Teacher training</span></li></ul>
      <div class="stack stack--xs"><p class="label label--plain">Showing all 7 projects</p><p class="pointer pointer--hang fs--1">A cross-reference or footnote, with a hanging indent so wrapped lines align with the text.</p></div>
    </div>
    {{ source('<span class="marker" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
<span class="marker marker--icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "check", "icon--l" %}</span>
<ul class="checklist" role="list"><li>{% icon "check" %}<span>…</span></li></ul>
<ul class="checklist checklist--dots" role="list"><li><span>…</span></li></ul>
<p class="label label--plain">12 photographs</p>
<p class="pointer pointer--hang">…</p>') }}

    <h3 class="sg-h3">Filter bar</h3>
    <div class="filter-bar">
      <div class="chips" role="group" aria-label="Example filter"><button class="chip" type="button" aria-pressed="true">All <span class="chip__count">7</span></button><button class="chip" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Water <span class="chip__count">4</span></button></div>
      <p class="label label--plain filter-bar__status" role="status">Showing all 7 projects</p>
    </div>
    {{ source('<div class="filter-bar js-only">
  <div class="chips" role="group" aria-label="…">…</div>
  <p class="label label--plain filter-bar__status" role="status">…</p>
</div>') }}
  </div>
</section>

{# ======================================================================= #}
<section class="sg-section" id="quote">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>Quote</h2>
    {% set quoteDemo %}
<figure class="quote">
  <blockquote><p>The hiti is not a relic. It is a functioning technology that still carries water.</p></blockquote>
  <figcaption>Hrishav Raj Joshi · <cite>field notes</cite></figcaption>
</figure>
    {% endset %}
    {{ quoteDemo | safe }}
    {{ source(quoteDemo) }}
